#!golden 1
#!case mc_getsysinfo_unknown_parameter
#!section exit
1
#!section stdout
#!section stderr
Invalid mc/bmc getsysinfo command: bogus
usage:
  getsysinfo <argument>
    Retrieves system info from BMC for given argument
  setsysinfo <argument> <string>
    Stores system info string for given argument to BMC

  Valid arguments are:
    system_fw_version   System firmware (e.g. BIOS) version
    primary_os_name     Primary operating system name
    os_name             Operating system name
    system_name         System Name of server(vendor dependent)
    delloem_os_version  Running version of operating system
    delloem_url         URL of BMC webserver

#!section requests
> netfn=0x2c lun=0x00 cmd=0x00 target_cmd=0x00 data=00
< rule=default ccode=0xc1 len=0 data=
> netfn=0x2c lun=0x00 cmd=0x00 target_cmd=0x00 data=03
< rule=default ccode=0xc1 len=0 data=
bye
